---
permalink: /tv/settings/
layout: layout.njk
title: TV board link
description: Build the address to point an arrivals screen at.
styles: ["/css/tv-settings.css"]
scripts: ["/js/tv-settings-form.js"]
---
{#
  Builds the address that configures a screen.

  Nothing here is saved anywhere: the fields feed one URL, and that URL is the
  whole configuration. Point a television at it and it is set up; point it at a
  different one and it is set up differently. Which is why this page is not
  meant to be opened on the television — build the link where there is a
  keyboard, and paste it in at the screen.

  Plain form controls, no framework, no fetch, no storage. There is nothing to
  save and no account that could be locked out.
#}
<main class="container container-sm settings">
  <h1>TV board link</h1>
  <p class="settings-intro">
    Fill this in on your computer, then set the address it produces as the
    television's home page. Everything the screen needs is in the link, so it
    survives a restart and can be moved to different hardware.
  </p>

  <form id="tv-settings" class="settings-form" novalidate>
    <section class="surface settings-card">
      <h2 class="settings-heading">Arrivals shown</h2>
      <p class="settings-note">
        Besides the large one at the top. More rows means a smaller countdown.
      </p>
      <label class="settings-label" for="rows">Rows under the big arrival</label>
      <select class="settings-control" id="rows" name="rows">
        <option value="0">None — just the next bus</option>
        <option value="1">1</option>
        <option value="2" selected>2</option>
        <option value="3">3</option>
        <option value="4">4</option>
      </select>
    </section>

    <section class="surface settings-card">
      <h2 class="settings-heading">Message</h2>
      <p class="settings-note">
        Scrolls along the top of the board, beside anything from the GPMetro
        service alerts feed. Leave it empty for no message.
      </p>
      <label class="settings-label" for="message">Message</label>
      <input
        class="settings-control"
        id="message"
        name="message"
        type="text"
        maxlength="200"
        autocomplete="off"
        placeholder="e.g. Elevator out of service until Friday"
      />

      {#
        The same three the feed uses, named by what they do on the board rather
        than by the GTFS words for them — whoever is setting this is choosing
        how loud to be, not filling in a spec.
      #}
      <label class="settings-label" for="severity">How urgent</label>
      <select class="settings-control" id="severity" name="severity">
        <option value="info">Information — blue</option>
        <option value="warning" selected>Warning — amber</option>
        <option value="severe">Severe — red</option>
      </select>

      {#
        The expiry itself is the date field; the dropdown only fills it in. That
        way "until Friday at six" is as easy to say as "four hours", and what is
        actually stored is visible rather than implied by a choice made earlier.
      #}
      <label class="settings-label" for="until">Show until</label>
      <input
        class="settings-control"
        id="until"
        name="until"
        type="datetime-local"
      />

      <label class="settings-label" for="duration">Or set it to</label>
      <select class="settings-control" id="duration" name="duration">
        <option value="">Choose a duration…</option>
        <option value="4">4 hours from now</option>
        <option value="24">24 hours from now</option>
        <option value="72">3 days from now</option>
        <option value="none">No end — until I remove it</option>
      </select>
      <p class="settings-note" id="message-status" role="status"></p>
    </section>

    <section class="surface settings-card">
      <h2 class="settings-heading">Board</h2>
      <label class="settings-label" for="stop">Stop number</label>
      <input
        class="settings-control"
        id="stop"
        name="stop"
        type="text"
        inputmode="numeric"
        autocomplete="off"
        placeholder="e.g. 1117"
      />
    </section>

    <section class="surface settings-card">
      <h2 class="settings-heading">The address</h2>
      <p class="settings-note">
        Set this as the television's home page. To change anything later, come
        back here and give it a new one.
      </p>
      <output class="settings-url" id="board-url"></output>

      <div class="settings-actions">
        <button class="btn btn-primary" type="button" id="copy-url">
          Copy address
        </button>
        <a class="btn btn-outline" id="open-board" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
          >Preview the board</a
        >
      </div>
      <p class="settings-note" id="copy-status" role="status"></p>
    </section>
  </form>
</main>
